Now I can see the problem clearly. At line 485-486:

```ts
if (options?.openMode === "new-tab") {
  openInNewTab(url, undefined, options?.breadcrumbStack);
  return;
}
```

When `handleOpenInNewTab` in `page-section.tsx` (line 722-728) calls:
```ts
openWorkspacePage(workspaceId, page.slug, {
  openMode: "new-tab",
  title: page.name,
  icon: page.icon,
});
```

The `openWorkspacePage` passes `undefined` as `headers` to `openInNewTab`, discarding `options.title` and `options.icon`. And since `options.breadcrumbStack` is also undefined, `openInNewTab` calls `buildColdStartBreadcrumb(url, undefined)` which produces breadcrumb items with default titles from the route registry.

The route registry for `/workspace/:workspaceId/pages/:pageSlug+` has `title: (p) => humanize(p.pageSlug.split("/").pop()!)` — which humanizes the slug. And the workspace ancestor would get `title: (p) => p.workspaceId` (raw ID again).

The fix: pass the headers (title/icon) to `openInNewTab` in `openWorkspacePage`:

