Now this fixes the page title in the breadcrumb for the leaf (page) item. But the workspace ancestor still shows the ID. The real issue is that `buildColdStartBreadcrumb` uses the registry title for ancestor items (which is `p.workspaceId`), and then `buildDerivedHeader` is supposed to resolve it using the workspace list.

Let me check if the workspace annotation is happening for the ancestor when building the cold-start breadcrumb for a page URL like `/workspace/:workspaceId/pages/:pageSlug+`:

Looking at `buildColdStartBreadcrumb` again: `deriveAncestorsFromPrefix("/workspace/:workspaceId/pages/:pageSlug+")` would produce:
- segments: ["workspace", ":workspaceId", "pages", ":pageSlug+"]
- i=3: candidate = "/workspace/:workspaceId/pages" → registered ✓ (not isContainer)
- i=2: candidate = "/workspace/:workspaceId" → registered ✓
- i=1: candidate = "/workspace" → not registered

So ancestors = ["/workspace/:workspaceId", "/workspace/:workspaceId/pages"]. At line 58, `/workspace/:workspaceId` IS annotated with `descriptorId: "workspace"`. So `buildDerivedHeader` should be able to find the workspace.

Wait, let me re-read `buildDerivedHeader`:

```ts
const [root, ...rest] = stack;
if (root.descriptorId === "workspace" && root.meta?.workspaceId) {
  const workspace = workspaces.find(item => item.id === root.meta?.workspaceId);
  if (workspace) {
    return { workspace, segments: rest.map(mapStackItemToSegment) };
  }
}
```

So if the root of the stack has `descriptorId === "workspace"`, it finds the workspace object and passes it to `DesktopBreadcrumbBar`. The breadcrumb bar then uses `workspace.name` for its root segment. This should work.

But wait — in the new tab case, `openInNewTab` creates the tab in the store. Then when the tab becomes active, `GlobalBreadcrumbShell` reads the breadcrumb stack and calls `buildDerivedHeader`. The breadcrumb stack should have the workspace root marked.

Let me check if there's something different about how the new tab's breadcrumb is read. Let me look at `openTab` in the tab store:

